Part of k224. Owner: unreagent-worker (cmd/launcher, internal/config; serial with other run() cards). Maintainer wants as the default path: create a project in Unreal, drop unreagent.exe in, start it — no config written by hand.

First step (scout, Linux, read-only): what the launcher does today when started with no unreagent.yaml, and with a config but no .uproject (only the WARN in cmd/launcher/main.go is known).

Acceptance: started in a directory holding exactly one .uproject and no config, the launcher runs with built-in defaults (project found, engine detected, agent started, toolkit bridge entry only when the plugin is present), logs one INFO line saying it runs on defaults and that "unreagent init" writes them out; several or no .uproject gives a clear error. Tests on Linux with a temp tree; Windows paths labelled unverified. Shares the default-building code with the init card — do this one first or together.

Scout result (Linux, code read plus runs of the Linux build in a temp dir):
- The config is searched only next to the executable (config.Load -> findConfig(exeDir())), not in the working directory. A missing file is fatal: "config not readable", exit 1, no hint.
- An empty unreagent.yaml is accepted but leaves agent.enabled, agent.claudeIntegration and mcp.enabled false (plain bools without defaults), so "no config" cannot mean "decode an empty document".
- Nothing in the file is required. Minimal working config today: agent {enabled, claudeIntegration} and mcp {enabled}.
- resolveProject takes the first *.uproject in the config dir, silently, when there are several.
- Nothing detects the toolkit plugin; the bridge exists only as an mcp.extraServers entry. README and skills use the flat path Plugins/UELLMToolkit/Resources/mcp-bridge/index.js, the example config the nested submodule path — detection has to search Plugins/ for Resources/mcp-bridge/index.js.
- Nothing notices an unbuilt project module (k229).
- Sub-commands: the subcommands map in cmd/launcher/main.go; hermes-setup is the precedent (k228).

Proposed hook, least change: in config.Load, when no explicit path is given and no config file exists, build the config from a synthesized default (a builder in internal/config that k228 reuses to emit YAML): agent.enabled, agent.claudeIntegration, mcp.enabled true; toolkit entry only when the bridge file is found; everything else through applyDefaults, resolveProject, resolveEngine, substitute, validate unchanged. Exactly-one-.uproject rule only on this path, so existing configs keep their behaviour. Info carries a flag; run() logs one INFO line. Engine detection functions (engine.go) are only called, not edited — low conflict with k211/k203.

Open: permissions on the defaults path (main agent proposes: off, as the built-in default is today — an interactive agent keeps Claude Code own prompts; maintainer may overrule); several plugin directories matching; the working directory on a double-click start (Windows, unmeasured).

Worker result (unreagent-worker, Linux). Tree is commit-ready, not committed.

Changed: internal/config/defaults.go (new: DefaultYAML, findBridges, loadDefaults, ToolkitServerName), internal/config/defaults_test.go (new), internal/config/config.go (Load -> load(explicitPath, dir); Info.Defaults; decodeYAML split into decodeYAML + decodeDoc), cmd/launcher/main.go (3 lines in run(): one INFO line).

Design choices (the worker's, not maintainer requirements):
- Shape of the builder: config.DefaultYAML(projectDir) returns the defaults as a portable YAML document (${PROJECT_DIR} in the bridge path, no machine path) plus the bridges found. The defaults path decodes that very document through the normal decoder, so a start without a config and a start with the file k228 writes cannot drift (pinned by TestDefaultYAMLRoundTrips). k228 writes the bytes, optionally under a header comment.
- Several toolkit bridges: pick deterministically (shallowest below Plugins/, then by name) and report all of them as one WARN through Info.Warnings; no error. Search is at most 4 directory levels below Plugins/, skipping hidden directories, node_modules, Binaries, Intermediate; a .uplugin is not required.
- unreagent.local.yaml is still overlaid on the defaults (so the engineRoot hint keeps working without a config), but unreal.project there is a load error on this path: the toolkit is looked up next to the launcher.
- Info.ConfigPath on the defaults path is the file that was looked for (keeps hermes-setup's local-overlay path working); the INFO line right below says it is not there.
- The INFO line does not mention "unreagent init": the sub-command does not exist before k228. k228 must extend the line.
- "Next to" means next to the executable, as for the config search today — not the working directory.

Permissions stay off on the defaults path (the built-in default). That is the main agent's choice, not a maintainer requirement; the maintainer may overrule.

Side effect to check in review: hermes-setup also goes through config.Load, so without a config it now reports "agent.hermes.enabled is not set" (or the no-.uproject error) instead of "config not readable".

